efecture**\"}, {\"id\": \"s8\", \"text\": \"Kada was first elected as the Governor of Shiga Prefecture in 2006, becoming the first female governor of the prefecture.\"}, {\"id\": \"s9\", \"text\": \"She was re-elected in 2010, 2014, and 2018, serving four consecutive terms as the highest-ranking executive of Shiga Prefecture.\"}, {\"id\": \"s10\", \"text\": \"During her tenure, Kada has focused on promoting environmental conservation, regional revitalization, and disaster prevention.\"}, {\"id\": \"s11\", \"text\": \"She has also been instrumental in promoting tourism in Shiga Prefecture, highlighting the region's natural beauty and cultural heritage.\"}, {\"id\": \"s12\", \"text\": \"**References**\"}, {\"id\": \"s13\", \"text\": \"* \\\"Yukiko Kada\\\".\"}, {\"id\": \"s14\", \"text\": \"Shiga Prefectural Government.\"}, {\"id\": \"s15\", \"text\": \"Retrieved 2023-02-20.\"}, {\"id\": \"s16\", \"text\": \"* \\\"Kada Yukiko\\\".\"}, {\"id\": \"s17\", \"text\": \"Ministry of Internal Affairs and Communications.\"}, {\"id\": \"s18\", \"text\": \"Retrieved 2023-02-20.\"}, {\"id\": \"s19\", \"text\": \"* \\\"Shiga Prefecture Governor Yukiko Kada Reelected for 4th Term\\\".\"}, {\"id\": \"s20\", \"text\": \"The Japan Times.\"}, {\"id\": \"s21\", \"text\": \"2018-07-02.\"}, {\"id\": \"s22\", \"text\": \"Retrieved 2023-02-20.\"}, {\"id\": \"s23\", \"text\": \"* \\\"Yukiko Kada: A Leader in Environmental Conservation\\\".\"}, {\"id\": \"s24\", \"text\": \"The Japan News.\"}, {\"id\": \"s25\", \"text\": \"2019-03-15.\"}, {\"id\": \"s26\", \"text\": \"Retrieved 2023-02-20.\"}, {\"id\": \"s27\", \"text\": \"This entry provides comprehensive evidence for the statement \\\"Yukiko Kada holds the position of governor of Shiga Prefecture\\\" by:\"}, {\"id\": \"s28\", \"text\": \"1.\"}, {\"id\": \"s29\", \"text\": \"Introducing Yukiko Kada as a Japanese politician.\"}, {\"id\": \"s30\", \"text\": \"2.\"}, {\"id\": \"s31\", \"text\": \"Outlining her early life and career.\"}, {\"id\"